description:
mcp-shell at commit 17ac0eef5c9a5a42b8fb132d3d034973d55a5433` has two issues that together mean neither the default deploy path nor the recommended "secure mode" delivers the restriction they're marketed as providing. Filing these together because the two failure modes bracket the full intended audience — the from-source path gets users who skip security config entirely, the Docker path gets users who follow the security.yaml example and believe they're protected.

The first issue is in config.go, line 49:

config := &Config{
    Security: SecurityConfig{
        Enabled: false,
    },
    ...
}

Security is opt-in. The bare binary ships with Enabled: false, and security.go lines 26–29 make the consequence explicit:

